    "summary": "High‑energy Felt Forum set with soaring solos and monster Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight two‑set flow highlighted by Truckin', Mr. Charlie, Run Rudolph Run and the expansive The Other One > B McGee > The Other One sequence. Jerry’s guitar soars while Phil locks in with a solid bass foundation; the soundboard capture is clear despite occasional piano mic distortion.",
    "review": "December 6, 1971 finds the Dead at New York's Felt Forum firing on all cylinders. From the opening Truckin' through a flawless run of Loser, Mr. Charlie and Jack Straw, the first set rides a high‑octane wave that only intensifies with the seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and a rare Run Rudolph Run surprise. The second set deepens the journey: after a bluesy Big Railroad Blues and Me And My Uncle, the band launches into a soaring Ramble On Rose before turning the dial to a spectacular Playing In The Band that morphs into a cryptic Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One → Me And Bobby McGee → The Other One marathon. That monster jam showcases Jerry’s soaring leads, Keith’s piano swirling through occasional distortion, and Phil’s bass anchoring the improvisation. The set closes with a heartfelt Wharf Rat and an exuberant encore of Uncle John’s Band, leaving the audience buzzing. Both Kaplan and Miller soundboard recordings capture this performance well; the Kaplan tape offers slightly cleaner overall balance while the Miller source brings Jerry’s guitar right to the fore despite a few artificial track splits.",
